{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 25, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a film that tells the story of the founding of facebook and the subsequent legal battles that followed. the movie is directed by david fincher and written by aaron sorkin, who is known for his witty and fast paced dialogue. the film stars jesse eisenberg as mark zuckerberg, the founder of facebook, and andrew garfield as eduardo saverin, zuckerberg's friend and business partner.\n\nthe movie begins with mark zuckerberg, a sophomore at harvard university, who is trying to get over a breakup with his girlfriend. he creates a website called facemash, which allows users to compare the photos of two students and vote on which one is more attractive. the site becomes a huge success, but also gets zuckerberg into trouble with the university.\n\nlater, zuckerberg is approached by twin brothers cameron and tyler winklevoss, who want him to create a social networking site for harvard students. zuckerberg agrees, but soon drops the project and creates his own site, thefacebook, with the help of his friend eduardo saverin. the site quickly gains popularity and spreads to other colleges and universities.\n\nas the site grows, zuckerberg and saverin become wealthy and famous, but their friendship begins to deteriorate. saverin is pushed out of the company and zuckerberg becomes the sole owner of facebook. the movie ends with zuckerberg settling a lawsuit with the winklevoss twins and saverin, and becoming one of the youngest billionaires in the world.\n\nthe social network is a well made film with great performances from the cast. jesse eisenberg is excellent as mark zuckerberg, and andrew garfield is also great as eduardo saverin. the film's script is witty and engaging, and the direction by david fincher is superb. the movie's score, composed by trent reznor and atticus ross, is also excellent and adds to the film's tension and atmosphere.\